      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Arteriovenous fistulas (AVFs) are infrequently seen in the civilian health-care system; traditionally, these lesions have been treated with ligation, or direct surgical repair with concomitant revascularization. We describe a rare case of a peroneal AVF treated with a stent-graft."},
